  "history": {
    "origins": "Xiàng Shí Fù is a traditional Chinese domino solitaire. The name means 'Watching Ten Sets'; it is also known as Cān Chán (參禪), meaning Zen. Play uses a standard 32-tile Chinese domino set; the aim is to rearrange the tiles into 10 valid triplets and one valid pair. English-language rules draw on contributions from Dmytro Polovinkin and Min Fanxin (闵凡信).",
